  "2026-10-27T02:27:06.270Z",codex-agent,"Auto-round-1 rules: bounded or failed verification cannot issue a positive certificate; an interrupted destructive plan whose validated preconditions changed must be superseded durably before a fresh exact set is authorized. Merge main completed and self-host verification passed. Audit covers erasure byte/native representation checks, integrity closure, GC reachability, checkpoint evidence and destructive receipts, including SDK/CLI and JSON/TOON surfaces. Plan recovery audit covers GC, compaction/unpack, erasure, working-tree pruning, ref retirement and bisect reset; raw owner cleanup remains bound to its original identity. CodeQL findings 32/33 are false positives for a constant shell program with quoted positional argv; paths are not evaluated as shell syntax. Replace the limit harness with direct argv-based resource setup to remove the flagged construction while preserving the Linux 128-descriptor soak. Add per-bound adversarial checks, changed-root/reachability crash recovery, real non-git trackers and isolated behavioral revert proofs; never close this item."
