  "2026-10-27T03:42:29.826Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof, auto-round-1: replacing only eraseFile with its merged-main-parent implementation makes the eight-recoverable-base64-layer regression fail 0/1 (Missing expected exception); restoring it passes 1/1, including loose and shared-pack representations. Replacing only prepareDestruction with its parent implementation makes the interrupted-GC/ref-change regression fail 0/1 with destructive_plan_conflict; restoring it passes 1/1. All fixed source was restored in finally blocks. Commands: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"eight recoverable\" test/erasure-accountability.test.ts; node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"interrupted GC supersedes\" test/gc.test.ts. Built and npm-packed Node/native Bun plus installed-CLI consumers now pass all 6 tests: the same SDK/command negative certification and GC supersession checks run across all five actual consumer scenarios; installed CLI checks both JSON and default TOON. The 32 MiB memory regression timed out under simultaneous consumers on the busy host and is being rerun serially without changing its assertions or timeout."
  "2026-10-27T03:51:34.119Z",codex-agent,"SDK capability recheck: the pinned public sdk/workspace-transaction.d.ts exposes commitWorkspaceTransaction(options): Promise<WorkspaceTransactionCommitResult> with audited text-file writes/deletes and item ids; it has no synchronous fd-bound compressed-range/pack intent operation. The package continues using that SDK for tracker mutations, locks/settings/history/rendering and native leases for synchronous storage. Public sdk/runtime.d.ts PmClient has no dispose(), drain(), close() or pendingWorkers() API; fixture-owned workers are joined and supported foreground settings are used. Open upstream searches for synchronous descriptor transactions and client worker disposal returned no matching issues; no new acceptance criterion is left unmet or package pin changed. Optional physical fingerprint transport is a package-owned ErasureDenial/bundle follow-up (pm-vcs-erasureprooftransport), not a missing PM SDK field. Public listAssuranceVerdicts has a bounded limit and no cursor; a full-cap result now refuses checkpoint certification instead of treating the newest page as complete evidence. The 32 MiB serial compatibility regression passed unchanged: retained buffers 1181841 bytes (below 8 MiB), all 32 unrelated native leaves preserved, selected leaf removed."
  "2026-10-27T03:56:24.473Z",codex-agent,"Verifier-class revert proof: an isolated module loader disabled only assertVerificationBound while leaving all real SDK and filesystem behavior intact. Five tests then failed 0/5 for the intended positive-certificate regressions: integrity reference_count retained verified objects, reachability object_count returned a candidate result, receipt record_count returned verified, accountability file_count returned a native certificate, and capped checkpoint history returned a receipt. Without the loader the same five tests pass 5/5. The full pm-linked bound suite passes 25/25; the separately linked native-copy/GC/checkpoint regressions pass 3/3. Recognized malformed or truncated encodings are negative outcomes; the old two-byte-zlib-header scanner expectation is strengthened from successful inspection to unverified/incomplete_stream, retaining its later complete-stream positive control. PmClient close(id, reason, options) is an item-closing mutation; the missing lifecycle capability is a client-disposal/pending-worker-drain API, not item close. Owner issue #151 teardown and ambient-agent test hermeticity remain in their separate landed commits. Full release gates remain unchanged and will run in CI on the pushed head; this item remains in_progress and is never closed."
  "2026-10-27T04:03:35.015Z",codex-agent,"Local implementation verification is complete: pm-linked verifier suite 25/25 and linked reported-regression suite 3/3; five shared-bound behavioral revert cases fail 0/5 and restore 5/5; two blocking-function reverts fail 0/1 each and restore 1/1 each. Built/packed Node and native Bun plus installed CLI pass 6/6; all 80000 descriptor reads pass at RLIMIT_NOFILE=128 with unchanged baseline 22; serial 32 MiB retention check passes unchanged. Supersession adds 128 seeded model transitions, 465 successor deletions, 68 native SIGKILL cuts and explicit old-handle/invalid-policy/completed-lifetime checks. Physical erasure now injects competitors at 9 boundaries (the prior 6 plus final physical scan), all passing; the truncated two-byte-header case now refuses unverified/incomplete_stream and retains the complete-stream positive control. Source typecheck, test typecheck, lint, zero-duplication and docstring gates pass. Focused coverage is still collecting the longer existing crash campaigns; final unchanged npm and Bun release gates will be checked in CI on the pushed head. Main is merged, PM histories retain byte-identical main prefixes, added lines pass privacy inspection. Relinquishing the claim for orchestrator verification while retaining in_progress; no item is closed."
  "2026-10-27T04:32:14.145Z",codex-agent,"Final fail-open audit found another instance of the same rule: the canonical member scan reused preflight unaccounted path exclusions during final verification. A different, fully native encoded copy recreated under a purged pathname can therefore evade representation inspection while passing native-format accounting. Add a fixed external-writer race with the generation and lock unchanged, require a pending denial and no success certificate, then prove retry converges after the copy is removed. Final inspection must use only current exclusions, never a historical purge list. This is a correction to the new verifier implementation; the current CI head will be superseded, not reported as final gate evidence."
  "2026-10-27T05:47:49.530Z",codex-agent,"Resume audit: current remote head is preserved; current main release/privacy changes are merged without changing dependency pins or publication policy. The final erasure certificate now couples complete native decoding, selected-payload inspection and raw-byte inspection to the same pinned descriptor, then revalidates the descriptor/path identity and whole catalogue. Purge preflight exclusions expire before final verification. Revert proofs: reverting only nativeObject to the previous format-only implementation makes the 32-cell loose/pack replacement matrix fail with Missing expected exception; the restored implementation passes all 32 cells plus 9 erasure-boundary cells. Moving payload hashing after the borrowed inspection feed makes the slot-mutation regression fail; restored hashing passes. The recreated purged-path fixed case also fails before the fix and passes after it. Streamed proofs reject incomplete/oversized ranges, sticky ignored errors, asynchronous callbacks and value-returning contracts; all 9 linked coupled-proof tests pass. The bounded 32 MiB erasure regression passes with 1,181,841 retained bytes and 52,228,096 RSS growth. Final built/packed Node and Bun consumers plus installed CLI and staged release fixture pass 8/8. Superseded CI was cancelled because the late replacement regression required a new head; it is not counted as full-gate evidence."
  "2026-10-27T05:51:30.302Z",codex-agent,"Merged-main validation passes 43/43 without skips or cancellations: release approval, staged release metadata, real tarball privacy and contaminated-session provenance. The source audit now covers 102 isolated entrypoints and 168 explicit allowlisted child launches across three embedded workers. Newly merged tests isolate sessions first; release fixture subprocesses use testEnvironment rather than ambient process.env. The package allowlist ships only the two required new consumer guides in addition to the existing public docs; scratch and benchmark evidence stay outside the npm tarball. Source/test typecheck, lint, zero duplication over all 88 production files, 547 documented declarations and strict emitted declaration consumption all pass. Owner issue 151 teardown and the original hermeticity fixes remain separate committed changes; the PR body retains Fixes #151."
  "2026-10-27T06:01:00.030Z",codex-agent,"Additional pre-push audit of superseded CI found two failures and neither is counted as passing evidence. The oversized-stat regression now asserts the stronger typed unverified/accountability/file_bytes result. The real authority regression was blanket worktree-erasure supersession: a retry could adopt a foreign replacement by pathname. Worktree erasure now retains its original inode authority across pending and completed receipts; generic validated object/reachability supersession remains available to GC and other owners that prove new eligibility. The original durable-denial replacement test and the new four-cell file/link x pending/completed property pass, including twelve repeated refusals and convergence after explicit foreign retirement. Revert proof: restoring only planErasure automatic eligibility supersession with a source loader makes the new property fail 0/1 (Missing expected exception); the real restored function passes within the three-test focused command. No existing regression assertions were removed or weakened."
  "2026-10-27T06:04:18.161Z",codex-agent,"Final narrow verifier campaign passes 36/36 with zero failures, skips or cancellations; focused diagnostics cover every added native-parser statement and all new helper functions. The earlier broad local campaign loaded a now-superseded test expectation and was stopped, not counted as a pass; historical full crash matrices remain covered by CI. The PM-linked ownership command passes 3/3. No full release suite was run locally. Final exact-head npm/Bun counts and CI links will be maintained in the already-linked PR 150 evidence section; dependency pins remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T07:16:26.299Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40459502820 on 72e597b completed the Node 22 npm suite with 2150/2154 passing, four failures, and 99.99/99.89/100/99.99 source coverage. This is failed evidence, not acceptance. Main introduced a direct scratch rmSync in the pack privacy verifier; it now uses the shared durability helper. Moving the existing complete physical-inventory consistency pass before supplemental diagnostics restores all three unchanged streaming inventory regressions, including exact second-pass assertions; the four failures now pass 4/4 locally. CI uncovered negative branches now have native adversarial cases for closure payload/time/fragment errors, operational receipt-clock failure, EOF-only decoding hits, revoked purge authority, invalid supersession policy, missing members/directory birth changes, and legacy CLI unverified reports. The focused new cases pass 10/10 with no SDK mocks or threshold changes. Further targeted coverage and behavioral revert proofs are being recorded before self-host publication."
  "2026-10-27T07:25:10.513Z",codex-agent,"CI follow-up validation: targeted coverage/regressions pass 23/23; the separately linked native check passes 14/14 after restoration, with zero skips/cancellations. All six real npm-pack privacy tests pass using durable cleanup; pack:check scans 312 shipped files with zero findings. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, zero duplication across 88 production files and all 547 declarations pass. Revert proof: restoring only verifyPack and eraseFile to their previous function behavior reproduces all four CI failures (0/4); restoration passes 4/4. Seven isolated function-level behavior reversions also fail their intended assertions: closure bound classification, receipt operational-clock propagation, final partial-quartet detection, directory-birth supersession, null-policy rejection, diagnostic failure refusal and legacy CLI negative verdicts. Each restored case passes in the targeted command. One early linked invocation overlapped the deliberately reverted cleanup function and detected it; the final serialized linked invocation passes 14/14. No regression assertion, coverage threshold or source inventory was weakened. The next pushed self-hosted head will rerun full npm/Bun CI."
  "2026-10-27T07:40:02.031Z",codex-agent,"Node 22.23.1 targeted follow-up passes 23/23 and confirms all new negative cases at the supported floor. Reading its LCOV beside the failed CI artifact identified one remaining regular-file identity comparison, distinct from directory birth. The existing supersession property now exercises unchanged and replaced regular-file and directory lifetimes, old-handle refusal, exact successor deletion and preservation of the retired originals. The Node 22 focused property passes 1/1 with nonzero hits for both directory and regular-file comparisons; the pinned-PM linked suite passes 14/14 after expansion. Revert proof: bypassing only the regular-file identity predicate makes that property fail 0/1 with resumed=true instead of false; restoration passes 1/1. Test typecheck and lint pass. This is a test-only expansion; production code, SDK contracts and thresholds are unchanged from 561ee4f. The validation head will be superseded by the committed self-host archive carrying this evidence."
  "2026-10-27T08:35:10.348Z",codex-agent,"Auto round 2 rule: physical namespace identity must be canonical and bound when a storage handle is constructed; inventory keys, durable intent members, leases and cache keys cannot mix cwd-relative paths with absolute authority. Reproduce the documented relative ObjectStore compaction, audit every matching namespace path across SDK/CLI and pack/loose maintenance, then test relative spellings, later cwd changes, crash recovery, packed Node/Bun consumers and renderer receipts on non-git trackers. Preserve all earlier class fixes and keep the item in_progress."
  "2026-10-27T09:35:10.151Z",codex-agent,"Auto-round-2 audit confirms the general invariant: physical path identity is captured at handle construction or API entry, and both inventory and durable deletion-set coordinates are normalized before comparison. Eleven filesystem-owning constructors, explicit range hints, lazy iterators, scan exclusions, returned purge authority and deletion aliases/journal paths were audited. The documented relative ObjectStore compact regression failed before the fix (zero objects, no pack, pending receipt) and passes after it. The complete 25-reader surface across four root spellings and all maintenance boundaries passed 27,000 live/erased checks. Built and packed npm Node and native Bun consumers plus project-installed CLI JSON/TOON passed 6/6; all use real non-git SDK trackers. Native relative-root SIGKILL sweeps passed all 13 compaction and 32 unpack boundaries so far; GC sweep and isolated behavioral revert proofs continue. Existing full npm release gate passed on the preceding head for Node 26; new-head CI remains required. No new review-thread findings were present beyond the supplied blocking finding; the two outdated CodeQL lifetime-launcher findings were already fixed, and current CodeQL reports no open alerts."
  "2026-10-27T09:50:35.942Z",codex-agent,"Auto-round-2 revert proof: 22 isolated behavioral reversions fail their targeted regression. These independently remove ObjectStore and PackStorage root binding; Repository, RefStore shared/private HEAD, OperationLog, RemoteStore, PublicationLeases, WorktreeMutation and FileTransport binding; lazy payload and inventory exclusion capture; explicit range/inventory hints and pack exclusions; accounting/scanner/purge root binding; deletion request aliases/journal binding; and the late caller-mutation refusal. The private ServedRepository constructor reversal separately fails the package-wide 11-owner structural invariant. Reversions execute only in isolated child module loaders, except the structural source probe which restores the exact file immediately. The initial private-HEAD fixture was strengthened to a distinct attached branch so both RefStore roots have discriminating behavioral coverage. After restoring all functions, the complete path suite passes 8/8 through pinned pm, the unchanged alias regression and compatibility set pass 8/8, and the complete relative reader matrix passes 1/1 with 27,000 checks. No existing assertion or threshold was weakened."
  "2026-10-27T09:50:39.137Z",codex-agent,"Auto-round-2 completed local evidence: documented relative ObjectStore now publishes a pack and a completed receipt. Eight path tests cover 32 seeded non-git stores, four spellings, 96 live identities, 4,032 cwd-changing publication boundaries, 74 exact-set interruption cases, four mutated namespace fields plus equivalent spellings, and explicit range/scan/purge/lazy-iterator binding. All 90 native relative-root SIGKILL cuts pass (13 compact, 32 unpack, 45 GC), with two completed replays per cut and no foreign-tree changes, duplicate identities or lost live objects. Additional reader matrix: 25 APIs, 540 boundaries, 27,000 live/erased checks. Real built and npm-packed Node/native Bun plus project-installed CLI JSON/TOON consumers pass 6/6. Compatibility passes 8/8, including 200 descriptor-lifetime cells; environment audit covers 103 test entrypoints and 170 child-launch sites. Source/test typecheck, lint, duplication (0 percent across 88 files) and docstrings (549) pass. Current main a31158d is included. Owner issue #151 remains fixed in aee95e4; ambient-agent hermeticity remains fixed in c56d797 and 1d372bd; PR body retains Fixes #151. Full npm/Bun evidence will be the new-head CI run; previous-head Linux npm gates passed on both Node 22 and 26, Windows GC passed 1/1 per runtime, and CodeQL had no open findings. Following the updated host rule, CI observation ends after at most 30 minutes after push if still pending; pending is not reported as a pass."
  "2026-10-27T09:56:51.672Z",codex-agent,"Implementation e2e751c is pushed with committed self-host acceptance exit 0. New implementation CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/40484609433 and CodeQL: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/40484609562 (queued at recording time, not passing evidence). This follow-up only records validation routing and releases the claim; its final pushed head re-runs CI. Follow the final head through https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/workflows/ci.yml?query=branch%3Afeat%2Findexed-pack-storage and PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/150. Final CI status and exact available counts are kept in the PR body and handoff. Full Linux npm and Bun suites may remain pending at the updated 30-minute observation limit; no pending gate is a pass. All local focused checks and 23 isolated reversions are recorded above, PM health and changelog pass, and the item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification. No merge, release or review-thread reply was performed."
  "2026-10-27T10:43:38.097Z",codex-agent,"Auto-round-3 rules: recovery authority must be durable through every ancestor before any destructive mutation; post-mutation source and destination namespace barriers must complete before acknowledgement. A retry must reconcile the original rename intent by its recorded immutable content and identity, even if its new temporary name differs. Audit all engine journal/publication/retirement sequences, preserve foreign records and legacy receipts, add namespace-loss fault injection at every boundary, and prove both regressions fail with only their fixes reverted."
  "2026-10-27T12:11:26.660Z",codex-agent,"Auto-round-3 audit: all engine namespace retirement routes share the platform durability backend. POSIX barriers now flush the containing directory and its complete ancestry; rename/link sources and destinations are fenced before publication and acknowledged afterward. Intent temporary cleanup also receives namespace barriers. Bootstrap format/index/link metadata and append-only operation retention evidence now flush file data before dependent publication or owner release. Publication authority uses one destination-derived key, validates its fresh input inside the lease, recovers the original immutable receipt under an id/authority CAS, and then snapshots the final replacement set. Existing pre-target-key receipts remain readable and recoverable; foreign records never become authority. The reported ancestry and original-receipt cases pass, as do acknowledged-log and bootstrap power-loss cases. The native fault model separately records file fsync and directory-entry fsync, drops unflushed entries/data on crash, retains inode identities, and verifies durable exact-set authority before every destructive syscall. It hashes complete persisted crash images (namespace, bytes, inode stamps); every raw boundary is covered, and only byte-identical images reuse the same proven recovery result. Current probes span 13 engine sequences, over 11,900 raw boundaries and roughly 1,500 distinct crash images. Two serial focused workers are restoring every distinct image and executing convergent engine reruns; no full local release suite is running."
  "2026-10-27T12:50:27.577Z",codex-agent,"Auto round 3 closes two general rules: recovery authority must have durable file bytes and every ancestor directory before a destructive syscall; interrupted publication retries must complete the original receipt. Audited engine unlink, rename, rmdir and fsync calls: all native mutations are confined to durability.ts. Added full-ancestry barriers, destination-keyed publication reconciliation with legacy receipt migration, and native power-loss modeling for metadata plus 13 write/retire sequences. The model additionally exposed empty ref/oplog/registry locks that cannot recover after a power cut; replacing these with flushed descriptor-owned process markers and strengthening the lost-ref-lease test to refuse before mutation. Existing success after losing a lease was inconsistent with the ownership requirement."
  "2026-10-27T12:58:32.164Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs for auto round 3: replacing only durability.directory with the previous single-directory flush makes the first-retirement ancestry regression fail (exit 1, durable journal ancestor missing). Restoring only the prior retireScoped and settleRetiredMembers functions makes the original-rename-receipt retry regression fail (exit 1, actual pending versus expected completed). Both fixes restored immediately. Targeted ref/oplog suite: 20 passed, zero failed. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, duplicate gate (zero clone pairs) and docstrings passed. Publication metadata and 13 native write/retire sequences remain under the full directory-entry/data-loss replay matrix."
  "2026-10-27T13:00:47.755Z",codex-agent,"The previous pushed-head CI completed with two stale test assumptions: invalid-input validation correctly creates no receipt directory, while that test unconditionally removed one; reader enumeration counted the private deterministic-lifetime generator as a new public reader. Strengthened the former to assert no directory side effect, and retained exact AST enumeration of all stream functions while separately asserting the two exported functions. Legacy source-keyed retry corpus passed all 8 owner-stamp/rename/replacement cases. Metadata power-loss replay passed all 142 native boundaries. Full current matrix is still running; no full local release gate is being started."
  "2026-10-27T13:28:18.300Z",codex-agent,"Native power-model revert proof: restore only the previous single-directory durability.directory body and run node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"EVERY native deep-intent\" test/journal-durability.test.ts. Exit 1: owner retirement lacks flushed recovery bytes and every ancestor. Restored the helper. The separate fresh control root and journal ancestry regression passes, as do all 17 competing-publication schedules, forced legacy enumeration bounds and native lease acquisition interleavings. Ref retirement/replacement previously passed 131 distinct crash images; source now also flushes both control and journal roots before owner publication, so affected full matrices are being repeated. The operation-log model uses its existing pre-publication validation callback for receipt deduplication under the native lease."
  "2026-10-27T15:39:13.097Z",codex-agent,"Additional class closure found by the native power matrix: a staging owner marker can be retired before its empty directory. Pack recovery now resumes only that original durable directory receipt, revalidates its inode lifetime under the intent lease, and reports completed peers truthfully. Foreign/replaced/nonempty entries are preserved. Eleven adversarial directory classes and sixteen peer-drainer boundary schedules pass. Publication recovery now validates action, single member and requested destination inside the receipt lease; copied receipt capabilities cannot certify a different write. Revert proofs: restoring only PackStorage.recover to b41f474 makes interrupted compact cleanup fail (directory remains); restoring only preparePlan makes copied-receipt validation fail (missing foreign_destructive_intent). Both exit 1, both restored. The optimized test model matches its uncached/full-scan oracle and resets mock histories per case; compaction passed 161 distinct crash images. Remaining full matrices are running with two serial workers."
